DISABLE WINDOWS UPDATE

The CineMassive configuration appears to be sensitive to driver changes.

The CineMassive driver installation also puts restrictions on driver updates through Group Policy to help prevent its drivers from being overwritten.

I disabled Windows Update to prevent Windows from automatically changing drivers or other components after the system was configured.

Windows 7 is no longer a supported operating system and should not normally be connected to the Internet.

NETWORK CONFIGURATION

My Alpha FX has two network adapters.

I configured Local Area Connection with the CineMassive internal network settings:

IP Address: 192.160.1.201
Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.0
Gateway: None
DNS: None

This adapter appears to be intended for communication between CineMassive components.

While in the properties for Local Area Connection, I unchecked Internet Protocol Version 6 (TCP/IPv6).

IPv6 caused problems in my setup.

I also disabled IPv6 on Local Area Connection 2 but left that adapter configured for DHCP.

Although connecting a Windows 7 computer directly to the Internet is not recommended, during my rebuild I temporarily used the second network adapter on my home network to simplify installation.

NOTE: Even if you are not connecting this system to a network Local Area Connection should be enabled and have a link light (be plugged into something).  Otherwise the IP Address 192.168.1.201 is not available and this breaks functionality.

